Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Matter contributions to the graviton self-energy", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ea18b485-5df7-449e-bfba-4f4444571a35"],

Cell["\<\
Explore scalar, Dirac fermion, massive-vector, massless-vector and SU(N) \
matter contributions. Each sector constructs tadpole and bubble terms, forms \
their stated sum, and examines its tensor structure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0913169-f191-495c-a02a-a20241999d3f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36e4b7e4-c248-4ad6-bd93-3b8eac7e68e0"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"343a6c8b-f813-467f-8277-ead69bf1c5c8"],

